  <ul class="small">
   <li>Wellness requires confirmation. Check-up also requires one year of continuous service. Pending, approved and paid claims consume the annual allowance. Submit only the reimbursable amount within the remaining limit.</li>
   <li>Use registered medical practitioners, dentists or licensed opticians. Dental cosmetic procedures and oral hygiene products are excluded. Optical covers spectacles or contact lenses; sunglasses, prescriptions and eye-care products are excluded. HR reviews receipts and coverage.</li>
   <li>Medical check-up is general body screening; denture, pregnancy testing, pre/postnatal and miscarriage expenses are excluded. HR must check the supporting receipt.</li>
   <li>Mileage: approved business travel in a personal car at RM0.50/km or motorcycle at RM0.20/km. Company vehicles and public transport do not qualify for mileage.</li>
   <li>Outstation meals: official duty in another city, more than 250 km return from the employment base. Submit each meal separately. Provided meals cannot be claimed. Missing meal receipts require justification; grade S requires a receipt.</li>
   <li>Wellness and check-up receipts are due by the 20th for month-end payroll processing. HR manages the cutoff and payment reference; claims do not automatically change payslips or transfer money.</li>
